{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1411","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Poman Numbers"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You've got a string $$$S$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ lowercase English letters from your friend. It turned out that this is a number written in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"poman"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numerals. The poman numeral system is long forgotten. All that's left is the algorithm to transform number from poman numerals to the numeral system familiar to us. Characters of $$$S$$$ are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ from left to right. Let's denote the value of $$$S$$$ as $$$f(S)$$$, it is defined as follows: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If $$$|S| \\gt 1$$$, an arbitrary integer $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le m \\lt |S|$$$) is chosen, and it is defined that $$$f(S) = -f(S[1, m]) + f(S[m + 1, |S|])$$$, where $$$S[l, r]$$$ denotes the substring of $$$S$$$ from the $$$l$$$-th to the $$$r$$$-th position, inclusively. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Otherwise $$$S = c$$$, where $$$c$$$ is some English letter. Then $$$f(S) = 2^{pos(c)}$$$, where $$$pos(c)$$$ is the position of letter $$$c$$$ in the alphabet ($$$pos($$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$) = 0$$$, $$$pos($$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$) = 25$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that $$$m$$$ is chosen independently on each step."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your friend thinks it is possible to get $$$f(S) = T$$$ by choosing the right $$$m$$$ on every step. Is he right?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$T$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 10^5$$$, $$$-10^{15} \\leq T \\leq 10^{15}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string $$$S$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ lowercase English letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it is possible to get the desired value. Otherwise, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can print each letter in any case (upper or lower)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 -1\nba\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n